// The DB export schedule lives in Windows Task Scheduler ("Dravya DB export"),
// not here. `cronTasks.tasks` used to duplicate it exactly -- same interpreter,
// same tools/export_db.py, same Sun+Wed 18:00 -- so whenever VS Code happened to
// be open at 18:00 both fired at once, and export_db.py takes no lock: two runs
// write schema.sql, manifest.json and the table dumps into the same directory
// concurrently. The scheduler also runs with the editor closed and records an
// exit code, which the editor cron cannot do.
//
// The "DB export" / "DB export check" entries in tasks.json are kept: they are
// still the way to run one by hand from the command palette.
